# TEMPLATE ONLY. Never compose-mount this file as the live broker ACL.
# Apply writes /opt/freedriver-secrets/mosquitto/acl (exact instance topics)
# and drops leftover freedriver/v1/home/... in that same write.
# Git must not ship __INSTANCE_ID__ or any fake id as the live ACL.
#
# Exact-topic ACLs. No wildcards, no $SYS, no +, no #.
# Never freedriver/v1/#. Never freedriver/v1/+/appliances or .../commands.
# instanceName is never a topic segment or ACL. Boards stay off MQTT.
# No C/DB plugin. No portal paste UI.
#
# instanceId is minted by the house (UUID hex+hyphens). Do not invent a
# UUID in git. Do not enforce a UUIDv4 version nibble. That already
# excludes /, +, #. kaze may hand the house-minted id to Techops:
#   INSTANCE_ID=<house-minted-uuid> ./scripts/provision-mosquitto.sh
#
# v1 one house: shared users autonomy and api, exact-topic only.
# api is not a wildcard superuser. No +/# bootstrap. A later instance
# gets its own autonomy user — do not share autonomy across instances.
#
# retain=false is a publisher rule. The broker cannot forbid retain.
# Publishers MUST set retain=false on both topics. Do not retain appliances.
# live-commands stays false. Do not open 1883.
# QoS 1 is a client convention; the broker does not enforce it.
# Quarkus does not SSH or restart Mosquitto.

user autonomy
topic write freedriver/v1/__INSTANCE_ID__/appliances
topic read freedriver/v1/__INSTANCE_ID__/commands

user api
topic read freedriver/v1/__INSTANCE_ID__/appliances
topic write freedriver/v1/__INSTANCE_ID__/commands
